  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">New Beginnings (GHANA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In northern Ghana life on the streets or in child labour is tough and addictive, and once out of school it is hard to get back in. This project will support children living on the streets and working in illegal goldmines and other dangerous exploitative situations. It will work with children who are at school but are being tempted or forced away.  The project will carefully reunite children and their families, then support them back into school or training.  It will work with the families to increase their ability to make a living through small loans, training and ongoing support &#x2013; ensuring that there is less pressure for children to leave home.  It will also work with teachers and health workers, as well as local decision makers, to ensure that children are welcomed back and provided with long term support to enable a new beginning.</narrative>
  </description>
